        (id: 204, board: "02", subject: "the archiver (alpha)", date: "06/28/1998", author: "eli", body: r#"
eli:
ok so i've been working on a thing. little daemon on node 4 that
reads the message base and indexes it. if the drive ever dies,
we don't lose us.

it does word frequency, reply graphs, who-talks-to-who, time of
day, typing speed, all that.

parallax:
"who-talks-to-who" is a weird thing to index, eli

eli:
it's for SCIENCE

mara:
it's running with my blessing. my reluctant blessing.

ghost_17:
can it index how many times crankshaft has said "beans"

eli:
412. as of tonight.
"#),
        (id: 205, board: "02", subject: "archiver update: it's doing something weird", date: "07/03/1998", author: "eli", body: r#"
eli:
so. the archiver is generating text now. i didn't tell it to.
it took the reply graph and started filling in replies that
nobody wrote yet.

one of them was a kestrel post. it sounded EXACTLY like kestrel.
pizza opinion and everything.

kestrel:
i'm flattered and also i want to go lie down

parallax:
turn it off.

eli:
it's not hurting anything. it's basically autocomplete.

parallax:
it's not autocomplete if it knows what i'm going to say about my
dad, eli.

eli:
...ok that one was weird. i'll look into it.
"#),
        (
            id: 206,
            board: "02",
            subject: "recover still works btw",
            date: "07/09/1998",
            author: "eli",
            body: r#"
eli:
for anyone who got CRC errors after the crash: i left {cyan}recover{/}
in the shell. {cyan}recover <file>{/} rebuilds sectors from slack space.
works on most stuff.

don't tell mara. she wants a "clean shell."

mara:
i can read this board, eli.

eli:
don't tell mara {b}again{/}.
"#,
            on_read: [If(NoFlag("cmd:recover"), [Set("cmd:recover"), Log("shell: recover available")], [])],
        ),
